  "observations": [
    "The board was running the candidate from the BENCH-COMMON-001 session; it was not reflashed. Its USB status reported ctl_hz=2000, armed=0.",
    "Initial configuration matched the reviewed baseline: P 2.5/2.5/2.0, every I and D zero, center 70, max 300/300/200, expo 0.5, deadband 8; also imu_lpf_hz 50.8346 and log_rate_divisor 1.",
    "roll-expo 1.1 exited 2 and the readback kept roll expo 0.5. The configurator rejected it host-side before sending; the firmware's own range check was not exercised.",
    "The temporary roll profile 60/250/0.4 read back in the same boot and after a cold USB power cycle, with every other value unchanged.",
    "The captured baseline validated, applied, and read back identically before and after a cold USB power cycle.",
    "The first `config show` failed with `device rejected config get roll_p: invalid command` after a serial monitor had held the port; the next command succeeded. cbc892b clears the parser only on USB deconfigure, not on a port close and reopen, so bytes left by another program still spoil one command.",
    "After the gate, log_rate_divisor was set to 2 as a separate change, so 2 kHz logging fits the store's 250 pages/s; the readback changed nothing else.",
    "The configurator annotates imu_lpf_hz with alpha 0.273 at a 1000 Hz loop rate; the board runs 2000 Hz. Firmware derives the coefficient from its own rate, so only the host annotation is wrong."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Cold boots were USB power cycles with actuator power disconnected; no brownout was induced.",
    "The operator reported completion without separate observations; no motor activity, arming or fault was reported."
  ],
